/-
# Abelian subgroups of 2-groups with cyclic centre (Kourovka Notebook Problem 3.28)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.28 (V. D. Mazurov): if `G` is a finite
`2`-group with cyclic centre and every abelian normal subgroup `2`-generated, then is every abelian
subgroup of `G` `3`-generated?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.PGroup

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.CyclicCentreTwoGroupAbelianRankKourovka3Problem28Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.28 (V. D.
Mazurov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700179 (`KOU-3.28`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

`k`-generated: the closure of a `Finset` of at most `k` elements; abelian by pairwise commutation.
-/

/-- Kourovka 3.28 (V. D. Mazurov): in a finite `2`-group with cyclic centre in which every abelian
normal subgroup can be generated by two elements, every abelian subgroup can be generated by three
elements. -/
def cyclicCentreTwoGroupAbelianThreeGenerated : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G], IsPGroup 2 G → IsCyclic (Subgroup.center G) →
    (∀ A : Subgroup G, A.Normal → (∀ x ∈ A, ∀ y ∈ A, x * y = y * x) →
      ∃ s : Finset G, s.card ≤ 2 ∧ Subgroup.closure (s : Set G) = A) →
    ∀ B : Subgroup G, (∀ x ∈ B, ∀ y ∈ B, x * y = y * x) →
      ∃ s : Finset G, s.card ≤ 3 ∧ Subgroup.closure (s : Set G) = B

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 3.28 "Not always", citing Berkovich (Algebra and Logic
9 (1970)): some finite `2`-group with cyclic centre whose abelian normal subgroups are `2`-generated
has an abelian subgroup that is not `3`-generated. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.),
Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026),
Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.28 (V. D. Mazurov); resolution: Ya. G. Berkovich, Algebra and
Logic 9 (1970), 75, Kourovka Archive, Problem 3.28: Not always, https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted cyclicCentreTwoGroupAbelianThreeGenerated_refuted :
    ¬ cyclicCentreTwoGroupAbelianThreeGenerated

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.CyclicCentreTwoGroupAbelianRankKourovka3Problem28Wanted
